{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:691981f6af05ad9dc5c6ab3ba826138bfe81c463b1dfa66d8136b2fb86f9fb9c","title":"How do scalar perturbations on a prescribed expanding background compare with perturbations that include the gravitational response of a scalar-driven universe? The comparison uses conformal time, a homogeneous background field, and distinct test-field and cosmological canonical variables.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69c751952a8db1d33b37105929f7c36ea0eef819126e14de43ef3cec3f8377d8","title":"Can two light geometric Kähler moduli surviving large-volume stabilization drive inflation with a noncanonical kinetic action, and how does their coupled curvature–isocurvature evolution modify the linear primordial spectrum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69a791d318757a8947129287c9a71d84857acb9a3be1526ba5386417f09507d0","title":"Can two-dimensional CDT incorporate controlled spatial and spacetime topology changes, and can a classical geometry with small fluctuations emerge from its background-independent path integral?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69ab822f9ef72c6e77724c7e855a82a64f800d947b2c9bd535fa649d760447bc","title":"Conditional on a string QCD axion solving strong CP naturally, should many additional ultralight axions exist, and how could cosmological observations and rotating black holes reveal their masses and couplings?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69e33d8ab92964159c5c8a2c49684a0b52e75cb1e71e37497ec534ffb561ccfb","title":"How does the near-horizon geometry control low-frequency retarded correlators, Fermi-surface excitations and possible instabilities of strongly coupled finite-density systems?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69c76d156cb620563e0bcda4c4219b65b68b63f4c351d8ec77d3ccdab52bfac6","title":"How do charge/spin responses and partially gauged theories distinguish selected bosonic SPT phases, particularly a 3D bulk's anomalous surface from a strictly 2D SPT with the same remaining symmetry?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69be19facfa996156c61f80ee76f314dd41c639239eb6b59ef63e0476ab6dd7f","title":"Does the proposed Big Fix maximum-entropy principle receive model evidence from late-universe radiation being maximized near the observed Higgs expectation value, when current quark masses, gauge couplings and the Higgs self-coupling are held fixed?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69b3a487be496c140ef5324a8bd1ffd3ffd1e1b1fe4708203d6e3c6f420f5920","title":"Does aligned natural inflation compatible with the multi-axion weak gravity conjecture generically acquire subleading potential modulations, and what oscillations and observational constraints follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0020"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:698f1b62513af38dcb3f5733bfc87119251b2347321c559e909c09f39845964c","title":"Do compactness of a bulk U(1) and modular invariance of its holographic CFT force charged states below the AdS3 black-hole threshold, and what additional constraints apply to residual ZN charge sectors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6985df2846fde07e8fecbfab9c16009f429dc7f1ba27ce858136236f03edffd5","title":"Can an attractive Gross–Pitaevskii system exhibit collapse after repeated trapped oscillations, and can independently varying resonance and nonlinear mode couplings clarify qualitative similarities with delayed collapse in AdS gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0023"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:699310f66928e77beb8526a3c154764a45ae1cafdf48f5fec6c4af44abcba441","title":"Could every nonsupersymmetric large-gap CFT descend from a supersymmetric parent through an RG flow? The source raises this conditional alternative without a classification argument.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:699d1c26b65d492cfd75f3e58dcb1b57fa7c5493217a577042353b61c637a9e9","title":"How can ten- or eleven-dimensional theories yield four-dimensional gauge and gravitational physics?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:692d8eaa290715317687d6f8fcbf5ab8ec8d7c913e8e264113aedf21b0733701","title":"Can the proposed swampland restrictions coexist with CMB-compatible single-field inflation? The paper adds scalar spectral tilt and potential curvature to earlier tensor-based comparisons, then tests whether DBI tensor suppression changes the conclusion.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69849e1cde0a380728ceb4c47aca9fb9866890c5f16f86d5fc9eddecbb03318c","title":"Can a common lower bound on inflationary and quintessence potential gradients connect primordial quantum fluctuations, present dark energy, and interacting dark matter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6951732a8a76f29a22bb5bb0c49e6436392cf48b6a3732ce799708589bbd5904","title":"How does continuous energy transfer from an inflaton to radiation change inflation compared with an effectively isolated inflaton? The bath can remain populated during accelerated expansion while potential energy dominates.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69d70b123e85b9b378facfc8b197a42cd7e7c7cd53a1f22478432c9880c619c9","title":"How can a heavy transverse field participate in inflation? Negative field-space curvature can destabilize ordinary slow roll and support a displaced turning trajectory in the imported minimal-geometry model.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69dabd06d2194c77c3866402676d41f895b69ad9d11eb1fc87c0920555fdd561","title":"Does spontaneous supersymmetry breaking on an evolving runaway scalar background give the true shifting goldstino an effective mass, and how does that mass depend on the potential, its slope scale, and mixing with other fermions? The analysis remains agnostic about de Sitter swampland conjectures.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69b0406f97454126e79dd34ee8eecd7b0d5b87ab85c6326e319fb25731b24e23","title":"What inconsistency follows from violating the scalar bound, how do formal extremal solutions become physical states, and how should the criterion extend to interacting scalars or other dimensions?","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69d038447a9890865532db22a99c4e9b1a4155160480492601f5d8b1cf9b0568","title":"Which scalar mediators can compete with gravity at the cosmological horizon? The proposal includes fields with m_varphi less than or of order H and excludes heavier fields from the horizon-force sum, giving a present-day threshold around 10^-33 eV.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69fc915848820d681dc16934e42fe3a889cd5d89b03473b2b1d8e85449d2c575","title":"What replaces canonical field distance and potential derivatives for a nonlinear scalar Lagrangian P(X,ϕ)? Normalizing the small-X expansion, temporal perturbations, or spatial perturbations produces different candidates away from slow roll.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:695618fa76a1b3b8b0ab7d4c253e794affb4e530cad9f0c30db55e92bd643172","title":"Can half-maximal truncations make dyonic ISO(7) supergravity tractable while retaining its important supersymmetric vacua, and what additional gaugings and AdS extrema arise?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6954917944305438f6219480665af41e506e78fb87635b6c6a695cdf6e49638a","title":"How do supersymmetric bulk couplings encode the tensions and interactions of strings and membranes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0054"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69f270c98e81101b783e5cd63fc048a3bc4eec580af7a072cd4eb4b872a68734","title":"Can a critical-string low-energy gravitational sector generate running-vacuum inflation without an external fundamental inflaton?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0056"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:69fc7cd5df79a6257f498f27f643d15272df50ab362de591d8b7afe89a2729fe","title":"What dynamics and observable signatures follow when bosonic dark matter has sufficiently high phase-space occupancy to behave as classical waves, and how can astrophysical observations and axion experiments test those signatures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0061"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"